<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56238" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καύνιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>from Caunus</i> (in Caria), <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.172
			</span></i>, etc.; ἡ K. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῦς</span>, of labour in vain—for this cow
			overturned the pail after being milked, <i><span class="en">
				<u>App.Prov.</u>
				3.6
			</span></i>; but K. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρως</span>, of illicit
			love, from <u>Caunus</u>, brother and lover of Byblis, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1402b3
			</span></i>.</div>
